{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness","id":413769,"title":"The Cosmology of the New World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-20T22:04:33-08:00","id":413769,"title":"The Cosmology of the New World of Darkness","content":"The cosmology of the nWod has always been a bit confusing to me. I decided to sit down tonight and try and create a visual map since I tend to learn better this way. Going around the web looking at other posts and whatnot, this is what I have so far. It would be great to get feedback and/or constructive criticism to keep this moving forward. A lot of my gaming friends would be giddy if they found something like this.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/BtIKZSb\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/BtIKZSb\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/BtIKZSb\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/BtIKZSb </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T22:16:30-08:00","id":413801,"title":"","content":"You've mislabeled the Shadow as Twilight, the Astral should by rights connect to/run through the Abyss at some point, the Emanations listed appear to be drawn ex nihilo and placed out of order with their relative position between the Supernal and the Abyss, the Underworld isn't a Lower Depth itself, and I'd recommend switching the layering between the Hedge and the arrow that I assume denotes its line of passage to indicate that it runs through the Abyss rather than being after it on a separate line of progression (fae cosmological elements' notorious fuzziness notwithstanding).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T22:21:17-08:00","id":413806,"title":"","content":"Circle labeled Twilight should be Shadow, I'd put either a black &amp; white or color inverted globe between the Material and the Guantlet to represent Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T01:20:44-08:00","id":413905,"title":"","content":"Ah, Mage cosmology. A topic dear to my heart. You've managed to lure this lurker out of the shadows.<br /> <br /> Last summer I couldn't stop thinking about the nWoD cosmology, and I knew it wouldn't go away until I wrote it down on paper. I feel it's pretty complete. My main game lines are Mage, Changeling, and Hunter. I haven't read Demon or Mummy yet so I might be missing a few things. The Dream Lands and Dark World are from Princess the Hopeful. Everything else on there is from the books.<br /> <br /> Looking at the map I should have flipped the positions of the Shadow and the Underworld, and the dividing line for the Underworld should be labeled as the Avernian Gates. I'll have to fix that and rescan the sheet. I'll try to do that tomorrow.<br /> <br /> If I'm missing anything feel free to point it out and I'll add it to the sheet if there's room.<br /> <br /> The Map: <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/lG6vocv.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.imgur.com/lG6vocv.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5123-ansgar","name":"Ansgar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T12:21:53-08:00","id":414255,"title":"","content":"Alright, here is attempt 2:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/BU7q88v\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/BU7q88v\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/BU7q88v\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/BU7q88v </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T12:33:14-08:00","id":414275,"title":"","content":"Looks better. This is the one I always liked: <a href=\"http://fc03.deviantart.net/fs70/i/2012/174/6/d/new_world_of_darkness_cosmology_map_drawing_by_willworks-d54kdaf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://fc03.deviantart.net/fs70/i/20...ks-d54kdaf.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T13:13:59-08:00","id":414374,"title":"","content":"I like that one, but making it so artsy also made it harder to read (I'm very much a function over looks person). There are strange things like Arcadia existing on the map three times. If he was still keeping it up maybe he could incorporate some of the other game lines as well. Still, the dude churned out a very attractive diagram.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T14:58:47-08:00","id":414469,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, why does everyone feel the need to label twilight? It is a state of being within the material realm rather than being its own independent realm. &quot;Twilight&quot; is just WoD slang for saying &quot;out of phase&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5110-shadow","name":"Shadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:03:33-08:00","id":414473,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they do not label solid, liquid or gaseous so labeling what amounts to another state of matter is weird. That said is a very, very common misconception the fact that Twilight is treated as another plane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:08:09-08:00","id":414481,"title":"","content":"I made mine semi-transparent just to indicate a veil you had to pierce between realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T21:04:54-08:00","id":414823,"title":"","content":"This was my attempt a while back. Didn't know about Duat at the time but it would have been in the lower depths. <a href=\"http://imgur.com/lepwGiV\" target=\"_blank\">http://imgur.com/lepwGiV</a><br /> <br /> Though to be honest if I were to make another chart it would be a circle with the Supernal (Empyrean?) at the center and would progress like this:<br /> (Empyrean?) -&gt; Supernal -&gt; Emanations -&gt; Abyss -&gt; Astral: (Anima Mundi/Dreamtime, Temenos, Oneiros) -&gt; Phenomenal/Fallen: (Material, Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, (Emanations?)) -&gt; Lower Depths: (Inferno, Duat, Strix, (Unknown?))<br /> Each -&gt; representing a step out from the center.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3323,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","user":"cmwatford","date":". 02-22-2015, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T00:53:47-08:00","id":414980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CthulusButtCheeks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness#post413769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be sad if you can't make it work 100%. The designers made the NWoD impossible to map on purpose.<br /> see:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In truth, we made some pretty deliberate decisions intended to make the various places defy mapping schemes. As I worked on Inferno, Astral Realms (Dreamtime), Dancers in the Dusk (The Skein section, among others) and Imperial Mysteries, you can blame me for designing these places to knowingly break comprehensive models.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong that the Cosmological WTFerry was the impetus behind me inventing those things? I remember sitting at lunch at my day-job at the time and thinking &quot;I know what'll upset people's maps!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T01:46:58-08:00","id":414986,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I've always been a bit leery of putting the Supernal realms as actual physical realms, but then I imagine them as a conceptual space rather a cosmological space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T02:01:47-08:00","id":414994,"title":"","content":"Aside from other quirks of my head-canon's cosmology, I envision the Empyrean to be sort of the cosmic bubble that wraps around everything else. Like, if all the different otherworlds were gumballs in a jar then the Empyrean is a blanket that's wraps the jar. It's not a glue or thread, so to speak, but more like skin on a human being: muscles hold bones and organs together, but it's skin that makes sure it's not spilling all over","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T04:55:32-08:00","id":415028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=414986#post414986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I've always been a bit leery of putting the Supernal realms as actual physical realms, but then I imagine them as a conceptual space rather a cosmological space.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In first edition, it was up in the air, but in second edition our decision to make the Supernal World what you see when using Mage Sight, and the Supernal <i>Realms</i> the unseen Supernal without the shape of the world to give it structure, has made it much clearer. The Supernal isn't a physical place, it <i>is</i> a conceptual space, and this has a few other knock-on effects; first ed Geist and Changeling flirted (changeling much more so) that Stygia and Mage Arcadia were in the Underworld and Changeling Arcadia.<br /> <br /> They're not. As of second edition, the &quot;Arcadia Question&quot; is answered with a great big No. The things that abduct people through the Hedge are not Supernal Fae, any more than the fuel Demons use is the Supernal World of the Obrimos. We considered the ramifications carefully, and decided that a long-teased crossover issue was an acceptable loss for the setting change we wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T05:17:19-08:00","id":415035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415028#post415028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In first edition, it was up in the air, but in second edition our decision to make the Supernal World what you see when using Mage Sight, and the Supernal <i>Realms</i> the unseen Supernal without the shape of the world to give it structure, has made it much clearer. The Supernal isn't a physical place, it <i>is</i> a conceptual space, and this has a few other knock-on effects; first ed Geist and Changeling flirted (changeling much more so) that Stygia and Mage Arcadia were in the Underworld and Changeling Arcadia.<br /> <br /> They're not. As of second edition, the &quot;Arcadia Question&quot; is answered with a great big No. The things that abduct people through the Hedge are not Supernal Fae, any more than the fuel Demons use is the Supernal World of the Obrimos. We considered the ramifications carefully, and decided that a long-teased crossover issue was an acceptable loss for the setting change we wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how I imagined it. Going to Changeling Arcadia vs. 'going to' Supernal Arcadia is &quot;I want to go to the Grand Canyon&quot; vs. &quot;I want to go to geology&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T05:17:44-08:00","id":415037,"title":"","content":"When I run Mage, I tend to only use Mage cosmology stuff. The reasoning being: Mage cosmology is very wide, and covers a vast amount of bases. I don't really like the use of stuff outside Mage if it can't be understood or examined by Mages because then it feels like everything is an exception to the way that the Arcana's cover all of the parts of reality. &quot;You have the power to influence the building blocks of creation! Except this. Or this. Or these over here. Or this stuff either...&quot; Kind of feels silly, you know? Everyone wants to take Mages out of their comfort zone with everything else in the setting.<br /> <br /> I like taking Mages outside of their comfort zone as well, but to do that I find the Abyss is the best way to do it. Perhaps something is vomited up from the anti-reality which simply works on rules from a different, no longer existing universe, and that throws everything out.<br /> <br /> This doesn't really cause me any problems because you can assume that the other WoD lines don't exist in a Mage game as the default, or the other way around, with no trouble. But I think if you say that Werewolves and Vampires and so on are all legends inspired by what little Sleepers recall of historical Mages. This might strike people as being somehow less interesting and complex than including anything, but I like a nice clean cosmology personally, and I think that you can do everything you want between the Supernal, the Astral Realms and the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T05:30:10-08:00","id":415047,"title":"","content":"Is the &quot;severed fragment&quot; interpretation still ok? <br /> <br /> Like, the fall wan't a clean break and the shadow and Faerie and underworld are sort of the bleeding stumps of their associated supernal realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T05:32:32-08:00","id":415050,"title":"","content":"I've always felt that the crossover compatibility was more trouble than it's worth. It created sacred cows that each gameline was discouraged to explore (Requiem and necromancy, despite the fact that ancient Greek ghosts were essentially blood-drinking spectres), and going with the crossover route (adding a Moros PC or NPC) would dilute the chronicle's central themes and mood.<br /> <br /> We mostly used Vampire cosmology stuff too. For example, Mages used the creative thaumaturgy from Blood Sorcery, same as Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T08:43:15-08:00","id":415184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415047#post415047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the &amp;quot;severed fragment&amp;quot; interpretation still ok? <br /> <br /> Like, the fall wan't a clean break and the shadow and Faerie and underworld are sort of the bleeding stumps of their associated supernal realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm misunderstanding the metaphor I think this interpretation still has the problem of implying the Supernal realms were, at least at one time, actual places that were &quot;cut off&quot; from the fallen world. An idea can't really have bleeding stump, or at least not one you can actually go to and interact with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:11:49-08:00","id":415240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415184#post415184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm misunderstanding the metaphor I think this interpretation still has the problem of implying the Supernal realms were, at least at one time, actual places that were &amp;quot;cut off&amp;quot; from the fallen world. An idea can't really have bleeding stump, or at least not one you can actually go to and interact with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree because of Supernal Verges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:43:28-08:00","id":415329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415028#post415028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not. As of second edition, the &quot;Arcadia Question&quot; is answered with a great big No.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Thank you.</i><br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Considering the cosmology of the World is not really mappable in any meaningful way, any map you make is fine. Wrong, but fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-22-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:17:53-08:00","id":415351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415329#post415329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Thank you.</i><br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Considering the cosmology of the World is not really mappable in any meaningful way, any map you make is fine. Wrong, but fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. By far my favorite WoD cosmology map I've seen was <i>super</i> wrong, but it was just so damn asthetically pleasing I didn't even care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","