"edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:40:16-08:00","id":415365,"title":"","content":"Damn this discussion got deep pretty quickly. I think I'll go with &quot;There is no spoon&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:44:23-08:00","id":415367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415351#post415351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. By far my favorite WoD cosmology map I've seen was <i>super</i> wrong, but it was just so damn asthetically pleasing I didn't even care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it that one that was full of stars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T10:53:38-08:00","id":415374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415367#post415367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it that one that was full of stars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might have been, I don't remember too many details about it. It looked like a scan right out of someone's notebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:14:36-08:00","id":415401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415240#post415240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree because of Supernal Verges.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except this is the other way around. These are &quot;supernal Elements imposed on aspects of the fallen world&quot; not &quot; bits of the supernal that were not excised during the fall&quot;. You could theoretically say that those other realms (the Shadow, Underworld, Arcadia) are areas where certain ideal of specific supernal realms are expressed more strongly, like a weaker verge, but they aren't remnants left behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 02-22-2015, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:28:31-08:00","id":415462,"title":"","content":"Isn't an idea coalesced to the point it acts like a physical space more or less what the supernal is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:39:55-08:00","id":415470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415462#post415462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't an idea coalesced to the point it acts like a physical space more or less what the supernal is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, kind of, but that coalesced physical space is the Fallen World. The Supernal is the idea(s) that the Fallen World embodies physically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-22-2015, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:49:51-08:00","id":415483,"title":"","content":"Well, no, but it <i>appears</i> to, to the mages that end up there by whatever means. Clearly the phenomenal has something of a solidifying effect on them. I mean, this is just wild conjecture, but isn't the idea that the less-than-mundane realms are some sort of vestige of the supernal archetypes that govern them at least <i>plausible</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T11:56:02-08:00","id":415503,"title":"","content":"When I say, here and in the Dev blog, that Mage Sight reveals the Supernal World, I don't just mean in the material world.<br /> <br /> Consider a Moros using his Sight to see Stygia while in the Underworld. Mages are <i>very</i> aware of the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T13:53:44-08:00","id":415623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415503#post415503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say, here and in the Dev blog, that Mage Sight reveals the Supernal World, I don't just mean in the material world.<br /> <br /> Consider a Moros using his Sight to see Stygia while in the Underworld. Mages are <i>very</i> aware of the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why, but the only image I can see is the mage screaming in horror....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:00:07-08:00","id":415630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415623#post415623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know why, but the only image I can see is the mage screaming in horror....</div> </div> </div> </div>Not compared to say.. if a Mastigos opened up his Mage Sight in the Inferno...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T14:39:51-08:00","id":415726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415483#post415483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, but it <i>appears</i> to, to the mages that end up there by whatever means. Clearly the phenomenal has something of a solidifying effect on them. I mean, this is just wild conjecture, but isn't the idea that the less-than-mundane realms are some sort of vestige of the supernal archetypes that govern them at least <i>plausible</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is more like this: imagine I have certain ideals concerning imagination and childhood innocence. I then use my considerable wealth garnered from my films to create a theme park that is a reflection of those ideals. At no point were these ideals physically there, nor is this park suddenly somewhere on the extension of reality between the physical world and those ideals. But if I walked through the park, I could see the overlay of my ideals much more easily than, say, Detroit (though I could still see elements there).<br /> <br /> That is the relationship I was talking about. The Supernal Symbols of the Primal Wild may be more active or present when a Thyrsus walks in the Shadow, and the sights of the other paths may be influenced by those symbols as well (The Obrimos see Symbols of power as taking the forms of beasts, etc). At no point was the Supernal and those realms connected more so than any other part of the fallen world, they are just the &quot;theme parks&quot;<br /> <br /> Supernal Verges are the step above, where those ideals have somehow become manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 02-22-2015, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:51:00-08:00","id":415966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415367#post415367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it that one that was full of stars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Went digging and found it again, and yep, that's the one. I'd forgotten it was you who posted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:13:00-08:00","id":415975,"title":"","content":"I thought it might be, because it was <i>so wrong</i> and yet <i>so pretty</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:16:54-08:00","id":415976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415630#post415630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not compared to say.. if a Mastigos opened up his Mage Sight in the Inferno...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this brings up an interesting question: does M2e still go with the notion that the Lower Depths are places where bits of the Supernal World are absent? E.g., if a Mastigos somehow ends up in the Inferno, is there anything there for his Mage Sight to reveal to him? Or maybe he\u2019s the only one who <i>does</i> see something there, while his Acanthus, Moros, Obrimos, and Thyrsus companions find themselves Supernally blinded? Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:19:22-08:00","id":415980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415976#post415976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this brings up an interesting question: does M2e still go with the notion that the Lower Depths are places where bits of the Supernal World are absent? E.g., if a Mastigos somehow ends up in the Inferno, is there anything there for his Mage Sight to reveal to him? Or maybe he\u2019s the only one who <i>does</i> see something there, while his Acanthus, Moros, Obrimos, and Thyrsus companions find themselves Supernally blinded? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that as SOME parts of the Supernal are missing. The Inferno is pretty close to the Fallen world, so I think it isn't all that deficient, when push comes to shove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T19:22:31-08:00","id":415982,"title":"","content":"Also, Emanations are still a thing: Supernal Verges are called \u201cverges\u201d because you can use them to cross the Abyss into an Emanation. If someone <i>wants</i> to play the \u201call cosmos are tied to <b>Mage</b>\u201d game, one could <i>almost</i> do it by saying that <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s Arcadian Realms are Emanations of <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-22-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T21:19:09-08:00","id":416131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415976#post415976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this brings up an interesting question: does M2e still go with the notion that the Lower Depths are places where bits of the Supernal World are absent? E.g., if a Mastigos somehow ends up in the Inferno, is there anything there for his Mage Sight to reveal to him? Or maybe he\u2019s the only one who <i>does</i> see something there, while his Acanthus, Moros, Obrimos, and Thyrsus companions find themselves Supernally blinded? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It somewhat irks me that it's taken that the Inferno and the Lower Depths are somewhat the same (as the same way every rhombus is a square and not vice versa). Inferno always struck me having something. Hate, Greed, Lust, Sin.<br /> <br /> These are concepts that have meaning and the Inferno just loves to spread them around (like an infection). Lower Depths to me is... less so. You're attempting to hit a man who isn't composed of Life or Matter. You're attempting to see without Forces or Mind. You're trying to eat a creature that doesn't have Death or Life.<br /> <br /> As much as the Abyss is Paradox, I see Lower Depths being Absence. And Inferno doesn't really sell it's self that way to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T21:31:16-08:00","id":416137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416131#post416131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as the Abyss is Paradox, I see Lower Depths being Absence. And Inferno doesn't really sell it's self that way to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, it's a part of the Depths. Wonder what it is it lacks..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:11:38-08:00","id":416153,"title":"","content":"Shock\u2019s point is that he doesn\u2019t think it <i>should</i> be part of the Depths. I tend to disagree, although I\u2019ll have to review <b>Inferno</b> to explain why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:27:08-08:00","id":416166,"title":"","content":"The Lower Depths especially has always been the part of the Mage &quot;map&quot; that is more &quot;I don't actually know what this is, and it's really weird, so let's call it a Lower Depth&quot; rather than a very carefully delineated and vigorously defined cosmological region. Their &quot;lack&quot; of some or all Supernal truth is a conjecture of Mage cosmologists, not necessarily what is &quot;really&quot; going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:40:31-08:00","id":416180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415401#post415401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except this is the other way around. These are &amp;quot;supernal Elements imposed on aspects of the fallen world&amp;quot; not &amp;quot; bits of the supernal that were not excised during the fall&amp;quot;. You could theoretically say that those other realms (the Shadow, Underworld, Arcadia) are areas where certain ideal of specific supernal realms are expressed more strongly, like a weaker verge, but they aren't remnants left behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main contention was with the idea that the Supernal is not a place you can go to. Although, it's less a place and more a state of existence, Supernal Verges being a place where the Supernal state of existence has super imposed itself on the Phenomenal. Supernal creatures can be translated from the Supernal and Archmasters can translate themselves to the Supernal. That seems like a place to me, at least in terms of being a &quot;point&quot; of arrival or destination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T22:46:23-08:00","id":416184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416137#post416137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, it's a part of the Depths. Wonder what it is it lacks..</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically it lacks a sense of empathetic other, right? Demons from Inferno are conniving, self-serving pricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:08:30-08:00","id":416202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416184#post416184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically it lacks a sense of empathetic other, right? Demons from Inferno are conniving, self-serving pricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the archetypes of the platonic form of everlasting tyranny are not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:22:08-08:00","id":416211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416202#post416202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the archetypes of the platonic form of everlasting tyranny are not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyranny is <i>a structure.</i> Being empowered by the willful contravention of divine law is kind of the <i>definition</i> of a core absence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-23-2015, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:45:43-08:00","id":416224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416211#post416211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tyranny is <i>a structure.</i> Being empowered by the willful contravention of divine law is kind of the <i>definition</i> of a core absence.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you arguing that the Exarch would be placed more according to the Lower Depths than the Supernal World given their particular flavor of oppression?<br /> <br /> Granted, they broke the world to be where they are but that would explain a bit how &quot;Paradise Broke&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:19:06-08:00","id":416248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416224#post416224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you arguing that the Exarch would be placed more according to the Lower Depths than the Supernal World given their particular flavor of oppression?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying that the actual things the Exarchs represent are not &quot;We broke the commandments&quot; and that is on a very basic level <i>what &quot;sin&quot; <b>is.</b></i><br /> <br /> The Exarchs are in some stories purported to be the prime example of hubris going unpunished. That is not their <i>defining nature</i>, and in fact the last word on the subject indicates that that part of them is the <i>most susceptible to erosion</i>. Regardless of whether the Ruin was ever the Atlantean king who cast down gods, she is eternally the pattern of civilizational entropy (which is not the same thing as an anti-civilization or the absence of civilization) that is the Exarch of Fate.<br /> <br /> The denizens of the Inferno are salved but not satisfied by human action that represents the <i>degrading of a moral structure.</i> The variety of ways this can be accomplished scarcely constitute a pattern in themselves, but that's the point of occult exaltation \u2014 giving the thing a name and form that it couldn't otherwise express.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:45:18-08:00","id":416261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416137#post416137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, it's a part of the Depths. Wonder what it is it lacks..</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtue.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Won't let me post without blather.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:03:31-08:00","id":416272,"title":"","content":"I think that the best way to understand what a Depth lack, is by seeing what it is &quot;eating&quot;- Inferno, for example, &quot;feeds&quot; when someone break her own moral code- that is, it &quot;eats&quot; morality and so that is the concept it lacks (some could be said about the realm of the strixs- they lack life, and so they eat them).<br /> <br /> Also, we need to remember that the divide between the types of realms is done by the Mages from their IC point of view. It is not that the Exrachs revealed themselves to the first mages, gave them a map and said &quot;you see all of those realms? there be dragons. do NOT go in there&quot;. Instead, mages has investigated many realms and discovered that their magic works weird in those places. Considering that the Supernal was placed &quot;high&quot;, those realms, in which the Supernal magic didn't worked well, were seen as &quot;low&quot; (the concept itself has started to form only during their Dark Era). I doubt that infernal demons by themselves recognize themselves as part of those &quot;lower depths&quot;- they are part of Inferno, and all others are competitors who want to eat their food.<br /> <br /> To conclude, I could see the same argument about whether a specific realm is a &quot;Lower Depth&quot;, what it lacks and how you define what it lacks as something mages do IC. Maybe, like Pluto,. one day someone from Mysterium would come and decide that Inferno is actually one of the Realm Invisible, creating a huge debate which would end with most of the Diamond Orders agreeing with him and the angry Free Council screaming &quot;don't take away our Inferno! we love it that way!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T01:47:38-08:00","id":416296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416248#post416248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am saying that the actual things the Exarchs represent are not &quot;We broke the commandments&quot; and that is on a very basic level <i>what &quot;sin&quot; <b>is.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I must make a detour. Given that RPGs are art forms, different interpretations happen.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs, as they currently stand, are the everlasting symbols of Pride, Arrogance, and Tyranny. Of which they cement the world in the Lie to supernaturally support and justify themselves (of which they use Awakened to do so) and it does appear that they have pushed out/caged/murdered several of the Old Gods to do so.<br /> <br /> At which point I must point out that that the Exarchs only skirted the issue &quot;We didn't break the commandments&quot; by murdering God and then attempting to redefining what sin is after the fact. Very nietzschean of them.<br /> <br /> I also can't help but to notice that there is a certain parallel of a figure of Pride storming the gates of paradise to kill his creator.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416248#post416248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exarchs are in some stories purported to be the prime example of hubris going unpunished. That is not their <i>defining nature</i>, and in fact the last word on the subject indicates that that part of them is the <i>most susceptible to erosion</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a game who's main theme is the temptation of man's power over the universe, and more importantly, his fellow man, I find this hard to believe. The Exarchs are quite the natural outcome of the worst that the Awaken abuses have to offer. Awakened hate them for their power, while secretly (or not, in the case of the Seers) envy them for it. They are the ever present enemy who the Mage may find himself reaching beyond himself and the game tries very, very hard to underline it's theme of power of man gone tyrannical which would be hard if they were first and foremost not Magi themselves at one time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416248#post416248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The denizens of the Inferno are salved but not satisfied by human action that represents the <i>degrading of a moral structure.</i> The variety of ways this can be accomplished scarcely constitute a pattern in themselves, but that's the point of occult exaltation \u2014 giving the thing a name and form that it couldn't otherwise express.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a point. Whispers and their ilk, yes. For others... Not so much. Several creatures in the back of the book hint at having their own defined names and one fallen angel makes an appearance.<br /> <br /> Of course this still begs the main question: Do the Exarchs even have a concept of an Empathic Other as it currently stands or have they &quot;degenerated&quot; down to the level of the moral level of the denizens of the Inferno when it comes to self serving amorality?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T02:06:16-08:00","id":416303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=416296#post416296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course this still begs the main question: Do the Exarchs even have a concept of an Empathic Other as it currently stands or have they &quot;degenerated&quot; down to the level of the moral level of the denizens of the Inferno when it comes to self serving amorality?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or do they even still have awareness on that level at all? After all, they are Symbols now. For all we know, the individual Exarchs might not have any more awareness of themselves and others than a storm or a rainfall. The signs, instructions and Ochema they send just side effects of their very nature, not grand plans. Perhaps the Exarchs cannot help doing what they do any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:23:17-08:00","id":416478,"title":"","content":"Or perhaps there are no Exarchs, and there never were. Mages, vampires, humans, mummies, angels of the God Machine, and many more things besides have always pursued self interest at the expense of others, and each time they do, they give more weight and power to the supernal symbols of tyranny which have always existed. Some mages have learned to call upon these symbols to empower the magic they use to prevent potential rivals from Awakening, and to make their Sleeper servants forget the magics being used to enslave them, (and of course to empower their self-serving magics) - but the more power they call on from these symbols, the more enslaved the mages become to them; after all, that's what tyranny <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs may just be a story mages tell themselves: for Seers to explain why as they call greater power they seem more beholden to it, why they have to keep taking from everyone even once they have everything;<br /> a story so that the Free Council can personify the system of tyranny in their rebellion against it - to give a sense that it is enforced from outside, not inherent to the world they believe in;<br /> and a story for all mages who, deep down, have the hope (and fear) that they could fundamentally rewrite the laws of the universe if they delve deep enough into the arcane","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:27:52-08:00","id":416506,"title":"","content":"With mage, it could well be that the Exarchs are both real ex-mage god things and supernal symbols the seers more or less invented <i>at the same time. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:06:42-08:00","id":416531,"title":"","content":"I was sharing the quotes from Malcolm and Dave about the cosmology being intentionally contradictory with a friend, and he said &quot;I suppose what I'm imagining is a box. Vampire opens the box, it contains a rabbit, 3 books, and a 50 dollar bill. Mage opens the box and it contains a small lion and a shoe. Both of them together open the box, and you end up with a lemur and a talking chipmunk.&quot;<br /> <br /> The discussion that followed resulted in us creating this box as a possible in-game artifact. I just wanted to let y'all know that this thread has spawned something <i>amazing</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 02-23-2015, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero