n-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T00:06:04-08:00","id":418456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=418403#post418403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm? What does that have to do with <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently the series has a box in it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T07:51:23-08:00","id":418728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=418403#post418403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm? What does that have to do with <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were referring to me, while it is under a different game system, it is still a good read in a very similar world environment. Quite a bit of time is spent discussing cosmology with many familiar terms between 1Ev2E. In particular I enjoued the way it really showed the different forms of applying the same force (magic) through technology vs waving your hands and chanting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:46:04-08:00","id":420902,"title":"","content":"Lower Depths - I know there is an official/ish statement that the Inferno is considered part of the Lower Depths, but this has felt forced to me, here is why (Apology for the word wall).<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths are supposed to be thin worlds - empty worlds. Often Lacking Arcana in whole cloth.<br /> While Inferno is definitely a broken realm, and lacks Virtue, the mechanics for its denizens are different from the two Lower Depths natives described in Mage supplements, which have nearly identical mechanics.<br /> <br /> Rather I place Inferno as a Verge. The entities of Thought must be cloaked in a True Name to sustain themselves. And are fed by Acts of Vice. (This aspect of feeding, does touch upon feeding on a soul just more indirectly - but mechanically feeds upon Willpower).<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths - Note from DavidB, writer of Seers of the Throne, the Tutor:<br /> &quot;Oh, and as the guy who inflicted the description of the Tutor on the world, this is what I had in mind...<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths, as I think of them, are as far from the Fallen World as the Fallen World is from the Supernal. They're not Abyssal - they're *empty*. A Thin Place, where strange things move through their grey void of a world taking in what few scraps of Mana they need to survive.<br /> <br /> The Tutor is undefined (to the point where you can't really perceive it) because it's not meant to be in this reality. It can't move by itself, or free itself from its half-materialized state because our world is just too *real* for it. It's functionally immortal because its home world (if its home can be said to be a world at all) is so far from Arcadia that Time doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> Imagine a world where the Ten Arcana don't exist - no Forces, no Death, no Spirit, no Life and so on - or are present in only tiny amounts due to the Supernal being so very far away. If it's hard to conceptualize - good. If a mage went there, they'd be like a Supernal being coming to the Fallen. That's what I was shooting for.&quot;<br /> /END Old DavidB QUOTE<br /> <br /> - Bunch of references about the Lower Depths...<br /> <br /> <b>Circumstantial evidence on WHERE the Lower Depths reside (Greek \u2013 Tartarus is below Hades' underworld:</b><br /> In Summoners it is stated that \u201c[Chthonians] allegedly know at least a little about the doorways to the Lower Depths situated in the deepest parts of the Underworld\u201d. - <b>Summoners</b>, p. 46 (i.e. that in in the deepest portions of the Underworld one can reach the Lower Depths). In <b>Seers of the Throne</b>, p. 217, \u201cThe Ministry now believes that the Tutor is a being from the Lower Depths, the distant and mysterious realm believed to be as far from the Fallen World as the Fallen World is from the Supernal.\u201d In <b>Tome of the Watchtowers </b>(p. 76) a story of the Breaking of the Celestial Ladder details an army of entities from the Lower Depths emerging into the world, and eventually later barred from the Fallen World by a bone portal in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Indications on WHAT/WHO dwells in the Lower Depths (Greek \u2013 Defeated titans, cyclopes, offensive mortals and their native jailers):</b><br /> In Summoner's, p. 62, it is suggested weakly, \u201cSome say demons \u2014 of the genuine 'demons from Hell' variety \u2014 dwell within the Lower Depths, believed to exist beneath even the Underworld\u201c. Further strongly suggested, \u201cOther Warlocks look [to Pandemonium] for information on 'true' Demons, the inhabitants of Lower Depths that, unlike the Demons of the Kingdom of Nightmares, feed on human vice and depravity.\u201d<br /> In Summoners p. 63 - \u201cthese beings [From the Lower Depths] are inimical to life. They despise all things with an intensity that rivals that of the creatures of the Abyss\u201d. This description is in fact contrary to the treatment the infernal demons receive in the book Inferno \u2013 those demons are, in fact, lovers of Vice, and a dead world would remove their most prolific sustenance.<br /> <br /> Paradoxically, the mortal dead, must free themselves from their fetters/passions/vices to descend to the deepest portions of the underworld. Is this why the Lower Depths were such a good prison? Or another contradiction?<br /> <br /> If the Demons and Angels of Inferno dwell within the Lower Depths, then WOD: Inferno's details about the Abyssal and Hell conflict applies: \u201cThe Abyss seeks a cosmos without meaning or form\u2014at least not in the way humans understand it\u2014but Hell relies upon the world, loves it even. The world is a furnace of sin, and demons warm themselves at it.\u201d<br /> <br /> This is the difference then between Abyssal entities and Demons. Abyssal entities are nihilists/corrupters if substance always, Demons want a total embrasure of Vice in all its forms, and want it to go on forever, not nihilism, but eternal degradation of the self.<br /> <br /> Two Explicit Mage Examples: \u2013 Tutor, Seer's of the Throne, p. 217-8, \u201cIt is a thaumivore, but it has another appetite as well: it eats the human sense of self.\u201d It does not manifest fully in the Material or Twilight, its form is heavily distorted.<br /> Decay, Summoner's p. 62, Ages/decays a space in seconds (Perhaps is converting Structure into Mana?), it speaks through the soul, not the mind. Acts as Acamoth and wants returned to its home. Has no physical form only its effects upon a space indicates its presence.<br /> <br /> Neither example consumes based upon acts of Vice, unless Decay is a demon of Pride and Tutor is a demon of Gluttony. This really infers a third class of imported entities, the condemned titans and cyclopes of Greek mythology, perhaps? Their manifestations are similar to low ranking Demons, but their range of power is much higher. One can alter the structure of a victim's soul, the other can grant powers.<br /> <br /> In WOD Virtues and Vice help one recover Willpower. How does this help an entity survive the Lower Depths?<br /> <br /> Demons and Angels (As described in Inferno) engage in extreme versions of their Virtues and Vices.<br /> They require extreme amounts of Essence, or a conduit to channel Essence to their forms.<br /> <br /> So mechanically and thematically I see the Lower Depths too worn out and alien to be the Inferno. Not saying it is not, just not how I see it, nor play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T00:51:00-08:00","id":421455,"title":"","content":"That's a lot of thought on the matter but I think you are forgetting something. The Lower Depths, while having some elements of comparison that mages and other entities(it's been somewhat implied that Duat is also one of the Lower Depths) can make, it's still really just a name Mages gave for some stuff they really don't understand. In game world it's probably a good bet that a lot of Mages and others that might study or at least attempt to study that subject, have to figure out if they really ARE similarities or they seeing patterns because they simply want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-27-2015, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T01:19:12-08:00","id":421467,"title":"","content":"Yeah... labeling something as being part of the Depths is the modern Mage equivalent of ancient cartographers marking, &quot;Here there be Dragons&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T02:01:30-08:00","id":421487,"title":"","content":"Oh, we're talking Lower Depths? Let me kindly post some stuff by Mr. Brookshaw:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Inferno is different in that it was always meant to be in the Depths</b><i>, afaik. We've just stated it with increasing clarity (which I'm actually quite glad of, now, because it lets Russell and Matt use it for Demon: The Frutang or not use it depending on if it fits - what's one *more* type of &quot;demon&quot; among friends?)</i><br /> ...<br /> <i>&quot;The Depths&quot; are a continuum of realms that lack the essential stability of the Fallen World and its associated cosmology.<br /> ...</i><br /> But, ultimately, &quot;the Lower Depths&quot; is a catch all term for &quot;off the map, and likes to eat us&quot;. The natives don't call their worlds that, if they call where they're from anything at all. The only reason the Shadow and Underworld aren't &quot;in the Depths&quot; to mages despute their also &quot;feeding&quot; from material reality is that Death and Spirit are Arcana. Explore far enough from the material world, and you reach worlds where mages' powers have limited or no utility because the Supernal doesn't influence local reality as much or at all. That scares mages, and when wizards are scared they give whatever it is a name so they can feel better about it.<br /> <br /> Here be Dragons. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T03:17:31-08:00","id":421535,"title":"","content":"Oh the irony of Mage, Cosmology &amp; &quot;Here Be Dragons&quot;...<br /> <br /> When all you have is Supernal Magic, everything looks like an Emanation...<br /> <br /> For example, I spied this elsewhere not too long ago;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/420806-is-there-any-connection-between-the-fall-of-werewolf-and-the-fall-of-mage?p=421373#post421373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think the idea of what &quot;Hell&quot; is has changed as nWoD has evolved, because now, &quot;Hell&quot;'s wherever a Demon sets up shop, and the concept of a &quot;demon&quot; in general is quite different, as well...<br /> <br /> But Vampires aren't really fueled by death, in any event. They're untouched by it. They in fact are noted for how little they tend to have to do with the dead or spirits. They are the ones that most fit the Mastigos archetype, as well.<br /> <br /> Basically, before Mummy overloaded it, you could argue a creature a reflection of each Supernal Realm:<br /> Aether - Promethian (by way of Stealing The Divine Fire)<br /> Pandemonium - Vampire<br /> Arcadia - Changeling<br /> Primal Wild - Werewolf<br /> Stygia - Geist</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage has always been about classic 'High Magic', drawing power from beyond this world.<br /> <br /> nMummy is explicitly 'Low Magic', using the natural power that flows in this world. Mummy is more akin to what we see in Second Sight (albeit, way more powerful) than any of the Realms, because it isn't 'foreign' like those realms. It belongs in the Fallen World because it is the magic of the Fallen World. This is my headcanon, not fact but it is also my answer to Mage cosmologists; Sekhem won't map to any of the realms because it doesn't belong to them, it's not an emanation of a Supernal Truth; it is 'native' birthed from the what we know as the 'Fallen World'. And any who try to factor it into a Supernal paradigm is going to run into some serious problems, just like if they tried it with the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> So who's to say that the Lower Depths do lack 'Supernal Elements'? Who's to say that isn't what the Awakened tell themselves to try and explain what they don't understand?<br /> They just have different rules, methods and position. They are an outside-context-problem in a manner that differs from the Abyss's nihilism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T03:30:19-08:00","id":421554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=421535#post421535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh the irony of Mage, Cosmology &amp; &quot;Here Be Dragons&quot;...<br /> <br /> When all you have is Supernal Magic, everything looks like an Emanation...<br /> <br /> For example, I spied this elsewhere not too long ago;<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage has always been about classic 'High Magic', drawing power from beyond this world.<br /> <br /> nMummy is explicitly 'Low Magic', using the natural power that flows in this world. Mummy is more akin to what we see in Second Sight (albeit, way more powerful) than any of the Realms, because it isn't 'foreign' like those realms. It belongs in the Fallen World because it is the magic of the Fallen World. This is my headcanon, not fact but it is also my answer to Mage cosmologists; Sekhem won't map to any of the realms because it doesn't belong to them, it's not an emanation of a Supernal Truth; it is 'native' birthed from the what we know as the 'Fallen World'. And any who try to factor it into a Supernal paradigm is going to run into some serious problems, just like if they tried it with the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> So who's to say that the Lower Depths do lack 'Supernal Elements'? Who's to say that isn't what the Awakened tell themselves to try and explain what they don't understand?<br /> They just have different rules, methods and position. They are an outside-context-problem in a manner that differs from the Abyss's nihilism</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you listen to the Mummy podcast or youtube from GenCon where CAS was spoiling some stuff for Mummy? If not yeah you hit the nail exactly on the head with your headcannon. He talks a bit about the NWoD cosmology niche that he wanted to use for the magic of Irem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T03:33:50-08:00","id":421557,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's basically my head-canon, too. Sekhem is the energy of <i>this</i> world, and Duat the Lower Depth wants it <i>bad</i> (or at least Ammut)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T04:30:41-08:00","id":421584,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T09:53:32-08:00","id":421906,"title":"","content":"From what it seems, the Lower Depths can be messed with, as long as you don't try to use the wrong arcana, the one whose symbols the realm lacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:40:58-08:00","id":422125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When all you have is Supernal Magic, everything looks like an Emanation... </div> </div> </div>Well, it is the basic premise of the game. The supernal is the underlying platonic reality of the world. Making lots of exceptions to that robs it of it's weight.<br /> <br /> I would add, that although Mummy in particular is meant to be very unplatonic; I don't think it actually works. It falls back into that platonic stuff really quickly. Sekhem can flow all it likes but it requires a pattern, and as soon as you have those patterns you're right back to platonism and the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T12:52:44-08:00","id":422134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422125#post422125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it is the basic premise of the game. The supernal is the underlying platonic reality of the world. Making lots of exceptions to that robs it of it's weight.<br /> <br /> I would add, that although Mummy in particular is meant to be very unplatonic; I don't think it actually works. It falls back into that platonic stuff really quickly. Sekhem can flow all it likes but it requires a pattern, and as soon as you have those patterns you're right back to platonism and the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mix Mummy and Mage, then Sekhem probably has symbols in the Supernal describing it. But they might well be the kind of symbols you don't mess with, that have basically achieved sentience, and any Mage trying to muck around with Sekhem by drawing on its Supernal representation is in for a bad time and a lot of pushback (the exact amount determined by whether you are putting mummies in Mage or mages in Mummy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:31:54-08:00","id":422149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422125#post422125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is the basic premise of the game. The supernal is the underlying platonic reality of the world. Making lots of exceptions to that robs it of it's weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or adds to the horror of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T13:44:51-08:00","id":422189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422149#post422149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or adds to the horror of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. At least I don't see how.<br /> &quot;there is this underlying code that supposedly consists of platonic ideals of things / symbols, but don't take it too seriously. You can't throw a stick without hitting an exception that somhow isn't covered&quot;<br /> Where is the horror in that?<br /> At some point even the most mystery loving Mage goes from &quot;oh fuck, why isn't this subject to the base code of the universe&quot; to &quot;another one? eh, thrown it on the pile with the others&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T14:34:59-08:00","id":422218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422189#post422189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point even the most mystery loving Mage goes from &quot;oh fuck, why isn't this subject to the base code of the universe&quot; to &quot;another one? eh, thrown it on the pile with the others&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww, cmon, it's only mummy that no dev has told us which arcana would be used to fiddle with them. We can interact with all other supernaturals and their powers through the appropriate arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T14:45:39-08:00","id":422224,"title":"","content":"It is a matter of how you like to see the World of Darkness as a whole.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the World of Darkness is so clouded in dark mystery and earthly and unearthly conspiracies that not even the Symbol Truths of reality have a firm hold on it. It plays into the idea that in the World of Darkness the truth is <i><b>not </b></i>out there. It is made up of infinite layers of secrets and lies. A new secret around every corner and if you are crazy or foolish enough to follow the rabbit down the hole you will spend chasing it forever. Not even the wisest Archmaster or most ancient Methuselah understands the World of Darkness fully.<br /> <br /> Now, you can argue that the above should not apply to mages, only to mortals (as I basically paraphrased the original WoD Core and GMC above), but mages are also Addicted to Mystery and addictions rarely end with the addict finding some final, blissful release. Well, unless you are morbid enough to count a Golden Shot.<br /> <br /> Besides, is there a better argument for the broken state of the world then the underlying &quot;code&quot; of reality not even covering it fully?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T14:53:58-08:00","id":422227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422224#post422224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a matter of how you like to see the World of Darkness as a whole.<br /> <br /> The idea is that the World of Darkness is so clouded in dark mystery and earthly and unearthly conspiracies that not even the Symbol Truths of reality have a firm hold on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they don't.<br /> I am not arguing against that.<br /> I am arguing against making said Symbol Truths a sad running joke.<br /> The Supernal doesn't need to be 'absolute', or somehow 'top' other gamelines. But for exceptions to matter they need to be exceptions, not the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422224#post422224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides, is there a better argument for the broken state of the world then the underlying &quot;code&quot; of reality not even covering it fully?</div> </div> </div> </div>lots of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 02-27-2015, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T14:56:18-08:00","id":422230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422227#post422227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no. They don't.<br /> I am not arguing against that.<br /> I am arguing against making said Symbol Truths a sad running joke.<br /> The Supernal doesn't need to be 'absolute', or somehow 'top' other gamelines. But for exceptions to matter they need to be exceptions, not the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>But where would you draw the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:01:17-08:00","id":422232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422125#post422125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it is the basic premise of the game. The supernal is the underlying platonic reality of the world. Making lots of exceptions to that robs it of it's weight.<br /> <br /> I would add, that although Mummy in particular is meant to be very unplatonic; I don't think it actually works. It falls back into that platonic stuff really quickly. Sekhem can flow all it likes but it requires a pattern, and as soon as you have those patterns you're right back to platonism and the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>During various discussions of 2nd edition changes, mechanics,etc. It's been mentioned Mage capacity to quickly, with the right stuff, recognizing the Supernal vs the non-Supernal. It really doesn't feel to me like Mages in the game setting are going to break down because non Supernal stuff is out there. Rather the opposite given the motivations to study things not understood. Even 1st edition dealt with the Mage's not completely sure of exactly what the relationship and reciprocations of influences the Supernal has with everything beyond. That doesn't say Mages cannot muck about with Skehem, Pillars,etc. It just means that if Mages ever found out anything concrete about the Deathless there would be interesting* mysterious to explore.<br /> <br /> *which is to say potentially insanity inducing, non euclidean, Nyarlathotop and shoggoth summoning, dark powers that stretch beyond time and space to before the beginning of the Universe Fhtang! mysteries..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-27-2015, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:02:55-08:00","id":422233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422230#post422230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But where would you draw the line?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll think about that when they hire me as Mage line developer. Until then, I'll leave drawing that line to DaveB.<br /> <br /> For this discussion I don't need to know exactly where I would hypothetically draw the line if I had to. I just need to know where I am absolutely sure that I wouldn't draw it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:37:32-08:00","id":422251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422232#post422232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> During various discussions of 2nd edition changes, mechanics,etc. It's been mentioned Mage capacity to quickly, with the right stuff, recognizing the Supernal vs the non-Supernal. It really doesn't feel to me like Mages in the game setting are going to break down because non Supernal stuff is out there. Rather the opposite given the motivations to study things not understood. Even 1st edition dealt with the Mage's not completely sure of exactly what the relationship and reciprocations of influences the Supernal has with everything beyond. That doesn't say Mages cannot muck about with Skehem, Pillars,etc. It just means that if Mages ever found out anything concrete about the Deathless there would be interesting* mysterious to explore.<br /> <br /> *which is to say potentially insanity inducing, non euclidean, Nyarlathotop and shoggoth summoning, dark powers that stretch beyond time and space to before the beginning of the Universe Fhtang! mysteries..</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you just said. The problem is we as outsiders/observers don't necessarily understand that. Not every pattern is a reflection of Above, if for no other reason than there is still a Below under the Fallen World. It's not that Mages can't understand the metaphysics involved with the other gameline, it's that trying to shoehorn it into a Supernal cosmology doesn't work very well. Part of the horror in M:tAw is that no matter how many mysteries you unravel, more terrible secrets lie hidden away. It is not the main theme, but it is one of them.<br /> <br /> Also just pointing out that the idea of the Supernal as the source of all magic of the Awakened is not universal amongst the Pentacle orders. There are factions of the Free Council who would argue against that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 02-27-2015, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:56:04-08:00","id":422270,"title":"","content":"Kinda/Sorta/Not quite.<br /> <br /> Okay. So. The Supernal World is everywhere, but only affects the Fallen World in spells, demesnes, Supernal Verges, or when a Supernal native or artifact falls (or is summoned) into gross reality.<br /> <br /> That does not mean that only those things register to Mage Sight, or respond to spells. Awakened magic doesn't <i>cause</i> the majority of Mysteries worth chasing, but it can certainly analyze and act upon them. The Empty Room isn't a Pandemonic Verge, and might never take a mage at all, but the victims show something weird in Pandemonium. Thyrsus Mages (very carefully!) observe Uratha shapeshifting while using their Mage Sight - the werewolf isn't the product of Supernal magic, but it's fascinating to watch from the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> A Mummy using an Utterance to transform into a swarm of scarabs will show up to a Mage looking for Life effects. A mummy using an Utterance to call down a meteor swarm will show up (big style) to Fate and Forces. Arisen bodies register as both alive and dead simultaneously, which is enough to turn any Awakened's head.<br /> <br /> The fact that mages cheerfully acknowledge that their tools didn't build everything out there in no way means that their tools aren't near-universal methods of studying phenomena. That's what magic's <i>for</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, Duat is semi-canonically (if you like crossovers) a Lower Depth, but so's where the Strix came from (and by extension the Kindred, if you believe the Strix are vampires' ancestors.) Doesn't mean a mage can't see through Obfuscate by warding off the mind-effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 02-27-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T15:59:24-08:00","id":422273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422251#post422251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with everything you just said. The problem is we as outsiders/observers don't necessarily understand that. Not every pattern is a reflection of Above, if for no other reason than there is still a Below under the Fallen World. It's not that Mages can't understand the metaphysics involved with the other gameline, it's that trying to shoehorn it into a Supernal cosmology doesn't work very well. Part of the horror in M:tAw is that no matter how many mysteries you unravel, more terrible secrets lie hidden away. It is not the main theme, but it is one of them.<br /> <br /> Also just pointing out that the idea of the Supernal as the source of all magic of the Awakened is not universal amongst the Pentacle orders. There are factions of the Free Council who would argue against that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I whole heartedly agree. I like the in world struggles, debates,etc that probably derive from certain parts of the Mage community on things like attempts to make the Supernal Theory of Everything but if it steps outside that to the OOC player base. Not so much....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:28:21-08:00","id":422295,"title":"","content":"The cosmology is hard to picture (a good thing I think). The Astral Realms for example, as you descend through your own soul, down through humanity's and the world's before reaching the shores of the abyss with the supernal shining from afar, the journey is more like descending through calculus, the real numbers and then the integers to see the purity of set theory in the distance (very mathematical, but the closest I could think of), and is in essence undepictable. I always loved how a mage can have an adventure by sitting there and meditating, going on a five session astral journey which externally took place in one evening, sitting in front of their fire.<br /> <br /> As for the Supernal Theory of Everything (nice phrase!), I think it's important to remember that a major insight for archmages is that the Supernal is not all there is, concept without form is empty and the Fallen World is full of surprises reflected in, but not purely derived from, its supernal code.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:46:26-08:00","id":422308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422189#post422189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point even the most mystery loving Mage goes from &quot;oh fuck, why isn't this subject to the base code of the universe&quot; to &quot;another one? eh, thrown it on the pile with the others&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this.<br /> <br /> As I said earlier, in my games Supernal magic covers everything. It's big enough that it can do that but leave plenty of room for mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:14:15-08:00","id":422376,"title":"","content":"I love the game, but I would prefer if there was material explaining how the different lines react to each other. Not everything has to be defined, but getting a framework in place would be nice.<br /> <br /> @Solar - same in my games. I've taken my cosmology and started adding house-rules for how they relate. My players are about to engage in multiple dimension hopping antics. Understanding their paths is very helpful from a GM standpoint. My campaign group has been running for the last three years and is a crossover; conflicting information is often an issue for me.<br /> <br /> I totally understand that some people prefer it unknown though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:38:57-08:00","id":422601,"title":"","content":"Even if The Supernal &quot;covers anything,&quot; that doesn't mean Mages can see it. Mages don't really understand the Supernal and its Mysteries; even Archmasters don't entirely. There could be, if you wish, a perfectly &quot;Supernal&quot; explanation for Werewolves that Mages just don't get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T21:48:21-08:00","id":422605,"title":"","content":"Regardless it's much of a muchness. The answer matters only at one place, the same place that reduces all of cannon to nothing more than suggestions: Your Table.<br /> <br /> We can all have our preferences and all be right. Truly that is a most excellent Supernal Emanation, Bill.<br /> <i>Right on, Ted. It's like, whoa, the entirety of existence is ever shifting to meet the whims of beings who see our reality as a pale reflection of their own.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T22:01:53-08:00","id":422619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://th01.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2012/174/6/d/new_world_of_darkness_cosmology_map_drawing_by_willworks-d54kdaf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://th01.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2012/174/6/d/new_world_of_darkness_cosmology_map_drawing_by_willworks-d54kdaf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://th01.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2012/174/6/d/new_world_of_darkness_cosmology_map_drawing_by_willworks-d54kdaf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://th01.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2012/174/6/d/new_world_of_darkness_cosmology_map_drawing_by_willworks-d54kdaf.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T22:34:45-08:00","id":422626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422218#post422218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awww, cmon, it's only mummy that no dev has told us which arcana would be used to fiddle with them. We can interact with all other supernaturals and their powers through the appropriate arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans. <i>Prometheans</i> and their Divine Fire are the exception that drives mages up the wall, because it\u2019s something that one would <i>think</i> would be covered by the Aether, but it <i>isn\u2019t</i>. <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> outlined which Arcana apply for every gameline that was out at the time it was published, <i>except <b>Promethean</b></i>. (Yes, we get a handful of spells that can interact with Pyros-related phenomena in very limited ways; but these are <i>themselves</i> exceptions to the rule. The fact that you can use, what, Prime and Mind? to injure a <i>qashmal</i> doesn\u2019t mean that you can use Prime and Mind to do <i>anything else</i> to <i>qashmallim</i>.)<br /> <br /> The interaction of Arcana and elements of <b>Mummy</b> are arguably not addressed simply due to a lack of opportunity to do so: the <b>Mummy</b> developers have firmly stated their lack of interest in addressing crossover issues, and no <b>Mage</b> supplements have been published since <b>Mummy</b> where it would be appropriate to address the issue. Ditto with <b>Demon</b>. But <b>Promethean</b> was deliberately <i>excluded</i> from a book that explicitly addressed every other major supernatural type that was out there at the time. <br /> <br /> Pyros need not be the <i>only</i> exception; if it turns out that Sekhem is indeed a mystical energy that utterly confounds mages the way Pyros does, I won\u2019t be heartbroken. But if that turns out to be the case, there will be <i>two</i> exceptions to the rule that mages can get a handle on practically anything. Not three, four, or \u201ctoss it on the pile with all the other \u2018exceptions\u2019\u201d. Still, my own <i>preference</i> is for <b>Promethean</b> to remain the sole exception here. <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think that the interaction between the <b>Mage</b> and <b>Mummy</b> metaphysics would be a fascinating thing to see explored: for instance, I\u2019ve seen suggestions that the five Pillars from <b>Mummy</b> might correlate well enough with the five aspects of the soul in <b>Mage</b> that the Subtle Arcana might map reasonably well to them. That alone would mean that interactions between <b>Mummy</b> and <b>Mage</b> can\u2019t be as straightforward as, say, \u201cthe go-to Arcana for dealing with <b>Werewolf</b> are Spirit and Life\u201d; so in that sense, it\u2019s exceptional \u2014 but it\u2019s kind of the opposite kind of exception from what <b>Promethean</b> has going: rather than \u201cSekhem is something that none of our tools are equipped to deal with\u201d, you get \u201cSekhem is something so complex that no <i>single</i> set of tools deals with everything\u201d. <br /> <br /> As for the Lower Depths: they aren\u2019t <i>merely</i> \u201chere be dragons\u201d; they\u2019re a particular <i>type</i> of \u201chere be dragons\u201d. They\u2019re the \u201cdragons\u201d that lack something that\u2019s found in the Fallen World, and feed on it because they crave what they\u2019re lacking. By contrast, the Abyss is a <i>different</i> kind of \u201chere be dragons\u201d that addresses things that are openly hostile to the Supernal World. But if something isn\u2019t parasitic toward the Fallen World or destructive toward the Supernal World and yet does not show an affinity for any of the Supernal Realms\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T22:58:37-08:00","id":422631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422601#post422601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if The Supernal &quot;covers anything,&quot; that doesn't mean Mages can see it. Mages don't really understand the Supernal and its Mysteries; even Archmasters don't entirely. There could be, if you wish, a perfectly &quot;Supernal&quot; explanation for Werewolves that Mages just don't get.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a fair amount of truth to this. <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> highlights the fact that there\u2019s more to the Supernal Realms than just the five Watchtower Realms that mages Awaken to; even the Archmasters are largely confined to a \u201cregion\u201d of the Supernal\u2019s conceptual space where the ten Arcana are dominant. And as vast as that \u201cregion\u201d is, it\u2019s still only one part of an infinite \u201cocean\u201d of Truth Symbols. \u221e - \u221e = \u221e. <br /> <br /> Generally, when I speak of \u201cSupernal\u201d, what I mean is \u201cthe <i>local</i> Supernal\u201d, where the ten Arcana of <b>Mage</b> hold sway. That\u2019s because if something isn\u2019t covered any of the ten Arcana or the Abyss, it doesn\u2019t really matter if it\u2019s \u201cfrom another part of the Supernal\u201d, \u201cfrom a (hypothetical) trans-Supernal Realm\u201d, or \u201ca part of the Phenomenal World that lacks any Supernal Truth-Symbol associations\u201d.<br /> <br /> I like to use the following image to help me envision the local Supernal Realms: <img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/31680834/star2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Bear in mind that this is <i>just</i> the Supernal Realms; it doesn\u2019t even address such things as Emanation Realms, let alone the Abyss or the Fallen World; and even in terms of the Supernal Realms, it\u2019s primarily limited to that portion of the Truth Symbols that correspond to the ten Arcana. <br /> <br /> To depict the relationship between this and the rest of the Tellurian (<b>Imperial Mysteries</b>\u2019 term for \u201ceverything\u201d), I\u2019d treat this image as the top layer of a stack, with the Emanations being the next layer down, followed by the Abyss, then the Astral Realms, the rest of the Fallen World, and finally the Lower Depths at the bottom. Maybe put the Underworld as a layer between the Fallen World and the Lower Depths; maybe not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-28-2015, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T05:18:59-08:00","id":422828,"title":"","content":"Something I seem to recall after looking through all this. <br /> <br /> I remember reading that some scientists now believe that the laws of physics we so painstakingly drew out? They now think all that stuff is just our local bylaws - if you get far enough out into the galaxy, or anywhere else, things change.<br /> <br /> So... yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T05:39:02-08:00","id":422831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422601#post422601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if The Supernal &quot;covers anything,&quot; that doesn't mean Mages can see it. Mages don't really understand the Supernal and its Mysteries; even Archmasters don't entirely. There could be, if you wish, a perfectly &quot;Supernal&quot; explanation for Werewolves that Mages just don't get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly when I run Mage, Werewolf Legends are made from stories about Mages, since they too can turn into Wolves and such. Uratha are a different kettle of fish and I love them dearly, but Mage to me doesn't need any of the other splats at all, it covers most supernatural concepts within itself. And if I ever need something terrifying and nightmarish and out of concept for Mages to deal with, then I have the infinite remains of broken realities that is the abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:16:35-08:00","id":423025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422828#post422828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I seem to recall after looking through all this. <br /> <br /> I remember reading that some scientists now believe that the laws of physics we so painstakingly drew out? They now think all that stuff is just our local bylaws - if you get far enough out into the galaxy, or anywhere else, things change.<br /> <br /> So... yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you hear that? Because I know it's pretty widely hypothesized that there are other <i>universes</i> that operate under different physical laws, but the laws of this universe, while nowhere near fully understood, seem to apply pretty consistently within the observable universe. Certainly within our own Galaxy, which is just down the block on a cosmic scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:15:16-08:00","id":423078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=423025#post423025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where did you hear that? Because I know it's pretty widely hypothesized that there are other <i>universes</i> that operate under different physical laws, but the laws of this universe, while nowhere near fully understood, seem to apply pretty consistently within the observable universe. Certainly within our own Galaxy, which is just down the block on a cosmic scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some recollection of what he's talking about. From articles such as; <a href=\"http://www.newscientist.com/article/dn19429-laws-of-physics-may-change-across-the-universe.html#.VPIE0vnF9kk\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.newscientist.com/article/...l#.VPIE0vnF9kk</a> or <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2010/09/100909004112.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases...0909004112.htm</a>, et al.<br /> <br /> Those are two quick searches, but I don't recall which articles I read a while ago, but it's an idea that's been discussed recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:32:05-08:00","id":423093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=422626#post422626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans. <i>Prometheans</i> and their Divine Fire are the exception that drives mages up the wall, because it\u2019s something that one would <i>think</i> would be covered by the Aether, but it <i>isn\u2019t</i>. <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> outlined which Arcana apply for every gameline that was out at the time it was published, <i>except <b>Promethean</b></i>. (Yes, we get a handful of spells that can interact with Pyros-related phenomena in very limited ways; but these are <i>themselves</i> exceptions to the rule. The fact that you can use, what, Prime and Mind? to injure a <i>qashmal</i> doesn\u2019t mean that you can use Prime and Mind to do <i>anything else</i> to <i>qashmallim</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was under the impression that Prime would be their key arcana. Now that you've said it, I didn't notice IM left Prometheans out.<br /> <br /> Given the whole idea behind their pyros coming from a place &quot;above&quot; the supernal, with raw information/creative power, there's some room for <i>more</i> prime shenanigans, if someone ever were to write about prometheans on a mage supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T10:35:48-08:00","id":423098,"title":"","content":"What dreaminggod said. Its been so long ago, I couldn't begin to pull up the original source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:25:03-08:00","id":423300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=423078#post423078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have some recollection of what he's talking about. From articles such as; <a href=\"http://www.newscientist.com/article/dn19429-laws-of-physics-may-change-across-the-universe.html#.VPIE0vnF9kk\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.newscientist.com/article/...l#.VPIE0vnF9kk</a> or <a href=\"http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2010/09/100909004112.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases...0909004112.htm</a>, et al.<br /> <br /> Those are two quick searches, but I don't recall which articles I read a while ago, but it's an idea that's been discussed recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty cool. Though it's a little misleading to say the implication is that the laws of physics aren't the same through the universe. It would just mean the value of alpha is not constant as we currently assume, which means anything dependent on alpha would function differently in different parts of the universe, according to the local value of alpha. So it's more that the laws of physics may be more complex than we currently assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:04:34-08:00","id":425207,"title":"","content":"If the Phenemonal World is the equal of the Supernal, both need each other (The Phenomal need the supernal to be conceptualized, the supernal need the phenomal to have a meaning) and the Lower Depths are the parts of the Phenomenal that lacks Supernal definition, does it means there is maybe some Supernal symbols that lacks phenomenal meaning and still manage to somewhat survive ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:10:47-08:00","id":425227,"title":"","content":"I would say the Phenomenal is to the Lower Depths as the Supernal is to the Phenomenal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:24:45-08:00","id":425238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425207#post425207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Phenemonal World is the equal of the Supernal, both need each other (The Phenomal need the supernal to be conceptualized, the supernal need the phenomal to have a meaning) and the Lower Depths are the parts of the Phenomenal that lacks Supernal definition, does it means there is maybe some Supernal symbols that lacks phenomenal meaning and still manage to somewhat survive ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:25:43-08:00","id":425239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=423300#post423300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is pretty cool. Though it's a little misleading to say the implication is that the laws of physics aren't the same through the universe. It would just mean the value of alpha is not constant as we currently assume, which means anything dependent on alpha would function differently in different parts of the universe, according to the local value of alpha. So it's more that the laws of physics may be more complex than we currently assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Misleading science titles for 500, please. But that's how it was reported, even if the actual findings are, of course, much more complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:45:17-08:00","id":425354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425207#post425207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Phenemonal World is the equal of the Supernal, both need each other (The Phenomal need the supernal to be conceptualized, the supernal need the phenomal to have a meaning) and the Lower Depths are the parts of the Phenomenal that lacks Supernal definition, does it means there is maybe some Supernal symbols that lacks phenomenal meaning and still manage to somewhat survive ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it's called &quot;algebra.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425227#post425227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the Phenomenal is to the Lower Depths as the Supernal is to the Phenomenal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plato's Cave is the quintessential (pun intended) analogy here.<br /> <br /> Supernal: the things walking around outside the cave.<br /> Phenomenal: the prisoners in the cave.<br /> Shadow: the shadows on the cave wall.<br /> Lower Depths: deeper in the cave, where less and less light penetrates.<br /> The Principle (of Promethean): The Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","user":"Xenu's Paradox","date":". 03-02-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:08:56-08:00","id":425374,"title":"","content":"It is, although I was thinking of Anathem by Neil Stephenson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:29:53-08:00","id":425412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425354#post425354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plato's Cave is the quintessential (pun intended) analogy here.<br /> <br /> Supernal: the things walking around outside the cave.<br /> Phenomenal: the prisoners in the cave.<br /> Shadow: the shadows on the cave wall.<br /> Lower Depths: deeper in the cave, where less and less light penetrates.<br /> The Principle (of Promethean): The Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> Plato's cave is useful, but it falls apart somewhat when we apply the cosmology to it, which I remind, <i>exists to confound models</i>.<br /> <br /> Within the basic understanding most mages run with, the Supernal is kind of both the world outside the cave and the sun, but of those two it's closer to the sun than simply the world, while the Fallen(Which includes not only the Shadow but the Hedge, Arcadia, the Underworld, and the Astral is the cave, while the Lower Depths are correct <i>maybe</i> if the lacking Arcana theory is true, which it might very well not.<br /> <br /> Archamages who have a broader view just find it more confusing. The relationship between the Supernal and the Phenomenal looks closer to the spiral of the Flesh(Mortal World) and the Shadow than the simple imposition of the sun and the cave(although it is still, functionally, exactly that), the hypothetical Empyrean they bat around as an idea is closer to the sun, the Astral becomes blurry in how to define it, the Lower Depths become definitively off the map rather than categorically definable by lacks, and The Principle, which might be from the Empyrean, nevertheless shows <i>a lot</i> of aspects indicating it's tied to the Phenomenal.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Principle is great <i>because it just doesn't fit into mage's model at any point of view</i>.v It's too creative to be boxed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:26:16-08:00","id":425444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425412#post425412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope.<br /> <br /> Plato's cave is useful, but it falls apart somewhat when we apply the cosmology to it, which I remind, <i>exists to confound models</i>.<br /> <br /> Within the basic understanding most mages run with, the Supernal is kind of both the world outside the cave and the sun, but of those two it's closer to the sun than simply the world, while the Fallen(Which includes not only the Shadow but the Hedge, Arcadia, the Underworld, and the Astral is the cave, while the Lower Depths are correct <i>maybe</i> if the lacking Arcana theory is true, which it might very well not.<br /> <br /> Archamages who have a broader view just find it more confusing. The relationship between the Supernal and the Phenomenal looks closer to the spiral of the Flesh(Mortal World) and the Shadow than the simple imposition of the sun and the cave(although it is still, functionally, exactly that), the hypothetical Empyrean they bat around as an idea is closer to the sun, the Astral becomes blurry in how to define it, the Lower Depths become definitively off the map rather than categorically definable by lacks, and The Principle, which might be from the Empyrean, nevertheless shows <i>a lot</i> of aspects indicating it's tied to the Phenomenal.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Principle is great <i>because it just doesn't fit into mage's model at any point of view</i>.v It's too creative to be boxed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Empyrean is the word I was trying to remember and misidentified with the Principle.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean = the Sun whereas the Principle is more like light. It pervades everything, giving it definition and meaning, and it's the presence of more or less Principle that defines Lower Depth-ness rather than a lack of Arcana.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean/Sun is the greatest source of Principle, but we can create pitiful imitations of the Empyrean in the form of Prometheans, carrying feeble sparks of Principle.<br /> <br /> Given that the Empyrean is the original source of human souls, and that the Abyss has cut the Phenomenal off from the Empyrean, the servants of the Principle (the Qashmallim) would necessarily take great interest in those who are kindling even the smallest flames of Principle within the Fallen world. Demiurges are quite literally the reason new human souls are coming into existence.<br /> <br /> Now go ahead and shoot this crackpot theory full of holes XD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T11:55:28-08:00","id":425481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=417340#post417340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b) they find a cat which is both dead and alive</div> </div> </div> </div>Schr\u00f6dinger the Mummy Cat?<br /> <br /> What Guild is he in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:15:51-08:00","id":425533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425481#post425481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Schr\u00f6dinger the Mummy Cat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Schr\u00f6dinger's Cat was probably old hat for any Mage that has ever Magesighted a Mummy.<br /> &quot;Both dead and alive? Yep, seen that&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, we really need a good, short verb for analyzing something with Magesight. If nothing else, either Mysterium or FC probably has jargon for that. DaveB, can we get that in 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:20:47-08:00","id":425536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425412#post425412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, the Principle is great <i>because it just doesn't fit into mage's model at any point of view</i>.v It's too creative to be boxed.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this still doesn't answer the real question.<br /> <br /> What's in the box?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:47:01-08:00","id":425550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425444#post425444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Empyrean is the word I was trying to remember and misidentified with the Principle.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean = the Sun whereas the Principle is more like light. It pervades everything, giving it definition and meaning, and it's the presence of more or less Principle that defines Lower Depth-ness rather than a lack of Arcana.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean/Sun is the greatest source of Principle, but we can create pitiful imitations of the Empyrean in the form of Prometheans, carrying feeble sparks of Principle.-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, except that's not true, for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean is only a theory, for starters.<br /> <br /> THe Principle is 'most likely' born from the collective wills of humanity throughout the ages as an expression of human creativity and drive. That sounds like consensus willworking there, but it doesn't explain where Pyros comes from or how it works, beyond the fact that it predominantly is found in the Fallen, but given that it creates souls, which supposedly come from the Supernal(and maybe the Empyrean if that isn't just a theory), it's questionable.<br /> <br /> Humanity is fucking awesome. I don't feel inclined to call even Prometheans pitiful imitations, because human is taking the Fire as far as we can, and the traces of humanity that remain with them goes the rest of the way into making a soul and true human life. That's really impressive.<br /> <br /> I'm going to stop on this subject, because while I think I might be a more level informant on the Principle because I don't place it above all else, I'm not as informed as the Promethean Regulars, so I'll let them go on at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T12:49:22-08:00","id":425557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425536#post425536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But this still doesn't answer the real question.<br /> <br /> What's in the box?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Jack in the Box's munchie pack, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:02:38-08:00","id":425580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425354#post425354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's called \u201calgebra.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Cute. But no; algebra, and mathematics in general, exists <i>all over the place</i> in the Phenomenal World. It\u2019s in such diverse intangibles as physics and music, the arrangement of flower petals, in architectural designs; and those are just the ones that popped into my head right off the bat. And don\u2019t forget what happens to such intangibles when you visit the Astral Realms. <br /> <br /> But getting back to the question that was posed: I think Suleri Drals is onto something here. Traditionally, the relationship between the Supernal and the Phenomenal has been presented as a hierarchy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425354#post425354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plato's Cave is the quintessential (pun intended) analogy here.<br /> <br /> Supernal: the things walking around outside the cave.<br /> Phenomenal: the prisoners in the cave.<br /> Shadow: the shadows on the cave wall.<br /> Lower Depths: deeper in the cave, where less and less light penetrates.<br /> Empyrean: The Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this layout, the Empyrean is at the most exalted point of the model, and you then descend through the Supernal into the Phenomenal and finally into the Lower Depths. But that model still presents connotations of the Supernal somehow being better or more real or in some other way superior to the Phenomenal, which is where <b>Mage</b> breaks from gnosticism. <br /> <br /> I think a better way to look at it might be as two sides of a mirror, centering around where the Abyss now resides: on one side, you have the Phenomenal World; on the other, you have the Supernal. On each side, you have three broad zones: one zone that\u2019s really close to the border and heavily influenced (one might even say \u201coverpowered\u201d) by the nature of the other side, one zone that\u2019s far away from the border and generally lacking any influence from the other side; and a \u201cgoldilocks zone\u201d where the other side\u2019s influence is felt, but not so much that its own nature suffers. <br /> <br /> On the Phenomenal side, the \u201cinner\u201d, \u201cmiddle\u201d, and \u201couter\u201d zones are the Astral Realms; the material world and its associated Realms Invisible; and the Lower Depths. The Astral Realms are the part of the Phenomenal that\u2019s Supernal-like, to the point that it\u2019s often hard to decide whether a given notion should be thought of as an Astral entity or as a Supernal symbol; the Lower Depths are the part of the Phenomenal where the Supernal\u2019s influence wanes, leaving its denizens starved for what the rest of the Phenomenal takes for granted. <br /> <br /> On the Supernal side, the \u201cinner\u201d, \u201cmiddle\u201d, and \u201couter\u201d zones are the Emanation Realms; the \u201cocean of symbols\u201d where you find various Dhatu, Exarchates, Cintimani, and so on; and the Empyrean. The Emanations are the part of the Supernal that\u2019s Phenomenal-like, to the point that you can visit them physically; and the Empyrean is the part of the Supernal that\u2019s so disconnected from the Phenomenal that it lacks any differentiation or diversity. <br /> <br /> IOW, something like this:<br /> <br /> [ Empyrean \u2190 Supernal \u2192 Emanations ][ Astral \u2190 Phenomenal \u2192 Lower Depths ]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:09:27-08:00","id":425592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425580#post425580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cute. But no; algebra, and mathematics in general, exists <i>all over the place</i> in the Phenomenal World. It\u2019s in such diverse intangibles as physics and music, the arrangement of flower petals, in architectural designs; and those are just the ones that popped into my head right off the bat. And don\u2019t forget what happens to such intangibles when you visit the Astral Realms.<br /> <br /> But getting back to the question that was posed: I think Suleri Drals is onto something here. Traditionally, the relationship between the Supernal and the Phenomenal has been presented as a hierarchy:<br /> <br /> In this layout, the Empyrean is at the most exalted point of the model, and you then descend through the Supernal into the Phenomenal and finally into the Lower Depths. But that model still presents connotations of the Supernal somehow being better or more real or in some other way superior to the Phenomenal, which is where <b>Mage</b> breaks from gnosticism.<br /> <br /> I think a better way to look at it might be as two sides of a mirror, centering around where the Abyss now resides: on one side, you have the Phenomenal World; on the other, you have the Supernal. On each side, you have three broad zones: one zone that\u2019s really close to the border and heavily influenced (one might even say \u201coverpowered\u201d) by the nature of the other side, one zone that\u2019s far away from the border and generally lacking any influence from the other side; and a \u201cgoldilocks zone\u201d where the other side\u2019s influence is felt, but not so much that its own nature suffers.<br /> <br /> On the Phenomenal side, the \u201cinner\u201d, \u201cmiddle\u201d, and \u201couter\u201d zones are the Astral Realms; the material world and its associated Realms Invisible; and the Lower Depths. The Astral Realms are the part of the Phenomenal that\u2019s Supernal-like, to the point that it\u2019s often hard to decide whether a given notion should be thought of as an Astral entity or as a Supernal symbol; the Lower Depths are the part of the Phenomenal where the Supernal\u2019s influence wanes, leaving its denizens starved for what the rest of the Phenomenal takes for granted.<br /> <br /> On the Supernal side, the \u201cinner\u201d, \u201cmiddle\u201d, and \u201couter\u201d zones are the Emanation Realms; the \u201cocean of symbols\u201d where you find various Dhatu, Exarchates, Cintimani, and so on; and the Empyrean. The Emanations are the part of the Supernal that\u2019s Phenomenal-like, to the point that you can visit them physically; and the Empyrean is the part of the Supernal that\u2019s so disconnected from the Phenomenal that it lacks any differentiation or diversity.<br /> <br /> IOW, something like this:<br /> <br /> [ Empyrean \u2190 Supernal \u2192 Emanations ][ Astral \u2190 Phenomenal \u2192 Lower Depths ]</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the single most sensical model I've seen yet.<br /> <br /> Which of course means that DaveB will specifically ensure 2e is incompatible with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T13:22:35-08:00","id":425605,"title":"","content":"Oh, certainly. Though I don\u2019t think that <b>Mage</b> will be the game to provide the inconsistencies to this particular model; I figure that games like <b>Promethean</b> and <b>Changeling</b> are better suited to such a task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:36:08-08:00","id":425735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425550#post425550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, except that's not true, for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean is only a theory, for starters.<br /> <br /> THe Principle is 'most likely' born from the collective wills of humanity throughout the ages as an expression of human creativity and drive. That sounds like consensus willworking there, but it doesn't explain where Pyros comes from or how it works, beyond the fact that it predominantly is found in the Fallen, but given that it creates souls, which supposedly come from the Supernal(and maybe the Empyrean if that isn't just a theory), it's questionable.<br /> <br /> Humanity is fucking awesome. I don't feel inclined to call even Prometheans pitiful imitations, because human is taking the Fire as far as we can, and the traces of humanity that remain with them goes the rest of the way into making a soul and true human life. That's really impressive.<br /> <br /> I'm going to stop on this subject, because while I think I might be a more level informant on the Principle because I don't place it above all else, I'm not as informed as the Promethean Regulars, so I'll let them go on at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to distinguish between theory and hypothesis. When you say the Empyrian is &quot;just a theory&quot;, you imply that the standard Awakened model of the cosmos is something other than a theory. But it is a theory, and could be overturned by a better model. The existence of the Empyrian is a hypothesis that seems to fit well within the standard model, except in the ways that it doesn't, and at any rate lacks sufficient evidence to be accepted by the Awakened community as a theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:14:57-08:00","id":425820,"title":"","content":"What is scary with idea of the Supernal being the equal of the Phenomenal is that maybe, it means the Supernal is not more uncorruptible and immune to the Abyss than the Phenomenal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:34:30-08:00","id":425825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425820#post425820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is scary with idea of the Supernal being the equal of the Phenomenal is that maybe, it means the Supernal is not more uncorruptible and immune to the Abyss than the Phenomenal...</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The light. We sought the golden light. You offered... The power of the Gods themselves. But it was... Black... Corrupt. Darkness... Ever since. How long?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:26:29-08:00","id":425937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425735#post425735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's important to distinguish between theory and hypothesis. When you say the Empyrian is &amp;quot;just a theory&amp;quot;, you imply that the standard Awakened model of the cosmos is something other than a theory. But it is a theory, and could be overturned by a better model. The existence of the Empyrian is a hypothesis that seems to fit well within the standard model, except in the ways that it doesn't, and at any rate lacks sufficient evidence to be accepted by the Awakened community as a theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main difference is that <i>the very existence of the Empyrean</i> is something unconfirmed, even by Archmasters; for <i>every other aspect of <b>Mage</b> cosmology</i>, the <i>existence</i> of the various Realms is not open for debate; only how they fit together. <br /> <br /> That said, I remember a time when the full extent of published material concerning the Lower Depths was basically a single sentence in the core book which implied but did not really confirm their existence, either. And until we got a look at the world through the eyes of the Archmasters, the <i>Supernal Realms</i> were often argued to be only theoretical. <br /> <br /> If my theory is right about the Empyrean being to the Supernal as the Lower Depths are to the Phenomenal, it\u2019s no wonder that not even Archmasters can confirm their existence, because <i>even they</i> are still tied to the Phenomenal World; and if the Empyrean is indeed that part of the Supernal that\u2019s largely untouched by the Phenomenal, then they can\u2019t go there, any more than mages can go to the Supermal Realms themselves. You\u2019d need to be Ascended to be able to enter the Empyrean, just like you need to be native to the Phenomenal to be able to enter the Lower Depths \u2014 and even then, the odds of your survival aren\u2019t good. <br /> <br /> I would also strongly recommend backing off of the common assumption that the Empyrean has something to do with <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s Principle. Even if it exists, the idea that the Principle is somehow related to it may still be nothing more than a theory by mages (or even archmasters) who are so disturbed by its failure to fit into their regular model that they\u2019re willing to posit that it comes from a \u201cplace\u201d on the Supernal side of the divide that\u2019s beyond their reach. As bothersome as <i>that</i> notion is, it\u2019s generally less bothersome than the notion that there are things in the Phenomenal World that aren\u2019t Abyssal which are <i>not</i> reflected in the Supernal. <i>That</i> breaks their model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T18:28:20-08:00","id":425938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suleri Drals</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425820#post425820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is scary with idea of the Supernal being the equal of the Phenomenal is that maybe, it means the Supernal is not more uncorruptible and immune to the Abyss than the Phenomenal...</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly not. It\u2019s just that the Abyss harms the Supernal in a different way than how it harms the Phenomenal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:04:28-08:00","id":426033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425937#post425937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main difference is that <i>the very existence of the Empyrean</i> is something unconfirmed, even by Archmasters; for <i>every other aspect of <b>Mage</b> cosmology</i>, the <i>existence</i> of the various Realms is not open for debate; only how they fit together. <br /> <br /> That said, I remember a time when the full extent of published material concerning the Lower Depths was basically a single sentence in the core book which implied but did not really confirm their existence, either. And until we got a look at the world through the eyes of the Archmasters, the <i>Supernal Realms</i> were often argued to be only theoretical. <br /> <br /> If my theory is right about the Empyrean being to the Supernal as the Lower Depths are to the Phenomenal, it\u2019s no wonder that not even Archmasters can confirm their existence, because <i>even they</i> are still tied to the Phenomenal World; and if the Empyrean is indeed that part of the Supernal that\u2019s largely untouched by the Phenomenal, then they can\u2019t go there, any more than mages can go to the Supermal Realms themselves. You\u2019d need to be Ascended to be able to enter the Empyrean, just like you need to be native to the Phenomenal to be able to enter the Lower Depths \u2014 and even then, the odds of your survival aren\u2019t good. <br /> <br /> I would also strongly recommend backing off of the common assumption that the Empyrean has something to do with <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s Principle. Even if it exists, the idea that the Principle is somehow related to it may still be nothing more than a theory by mages (or even archmasters) who are so disturbed by its failure to fit into their regular model that they\u2019re willing to posit that it comes from a \u201cplace\u201d on the Supernal side of the divide that\u2019s beyond their reach. As bothersome as <i>that</i> notion is, it\u2019s generally less bothersome than the notion that there are things in the Phenomenal World that aren\u2019t Abyssal which are <i>not</i> reflected in the Supernal. <i>That</i> breaks their model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. I was just talking about terminology. People often use the words theory and hypothesis interchangably, but their actual meanings could not be further from each other. A hypothesis is an educated guess, and it's what most laymen actually mean when they say &quot;I have a theory.&quot; A theory is an explanation for observable phenomenon that has been thoroughly tested and is well supported by empirical evidence, and is accepted by the scientific community as, essentially. fact - unless new evidence is found that challenges the assumptions the theory is founded on. So when people say something is &quot;just a theory&quot;, they me it sound like oh, that's just one possible explanation, we don't really know if it's true... Well, yes, but we never know anything with absolute certainty, and the word Theory is reserved for things that we are as close to certain of as possible, given the available evidence. So something untestable and unvarafiable like the Empyrian would be better described as a hypothesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T19:35:45-08:00","id":426057,"title":"","content":"Ah. Well, most of us around here are laymen; so I\u2019m not surprised that the layman\u2019s definition of \u201ctheory\u201d tends to get used. <br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019m inclined to view the Empyrean as part of a theory (in your preferred sense of the term) rather than a hypothesis: in particular, the interdependence of the Supernal and the Phenomenal (as opposed to a hierarchal dependence of the Phenomenal on the Supernal) has strong evidentiary support (e.g., the need to prepare the Phenomenal to accept changes to the Supernal before said changes can take hold); and the symmetry of that situation combined with the confirmed existence of Abaddon (i.e., parts of the Phenomenal that are too distant from the Supernal for any appreciable connection to exist, to the detriment of said parts) strongly implies a parallel situation on the other side. And the implications of what a part of the Supernal would look like without any substantial influence from the Phenomenal fit very closely with what we\u2019ve been told of the Empyrean. <br /> <br /> So although nobody has firsthand experience of the Empyrean, its existence and nature is a logical inference of a theory that covers most of the remaining known facts. Even the relative lack of firsthand experience is addressed. So to me, the Empyrean is more theoretical than it is hypothetical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T21:51:50-08:00","id":426166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425735#post425735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's important to distinguish between theory and hypothesis. When you say the Empyrian is &quot;just a theory&quot;, you imply that the standard Awakened model of the cosmos is something other than a theory. But it is a theory, and could be overturned by a better model. The existence of the Empyrian is a hypothesis that seems to fit well within the standard model, except in the ways that it doesn't, and at any rate lacks sufficient evidence to be accepted by the Awakened community as a theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm an Creative Writing English major, I deal in colloquialisms and broad semantics, not scientifically precise phrasing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T00:16:57-08:00","id":426255,"title":"","content":"It still remains an unclassifiable element : the place where souls go to die","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T06:37:57-08:00","id":426513,"title":"","content":"Umm...did the Empyrean somehow become a cannon place? Last time I checked, there was no mention in any book beyond Inferno, and even that book never confirmed that the Empyrean angels weren't simply another name for God Machine angels, qashmallim, or Supernal Cherubim / Seraphim. If we can have multiple different things use the same name, I don't see any reason why one thing can't have multiple names.<br /> <br /> Seriously, have I missed something beyond that one sidebar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T07:37:52-08:00","id":426566,"title":"","content":"Imperial Mysteries actually, I came across it while skimming through it a short while ago.<br /> <br /> Page 53, a speculated place but yeah it's name dropped there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-03-2015, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T08:17:05-08:00","id":426586,"title":"","content":"For the record, I\u2019m using \u201cEmpyrean\u201d in the sense that\u2019s used in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, not as it\u2019s used in <b>Inferno</b> (they\u2019re compatible, but not necessarily the same).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T10:02:37-08:00","id":426650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=425536#post425536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this still doesn't answer the real question.<br /> <br /> What's in the box?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think the right answer is &quot;three pounds of flax&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T10:16:11-08:00","id":426665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=426650#post426650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think the right answer is &quot;three pounds of flax&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly, it's Gwyneth Paltrow's head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T12:50:19-08:00","id":426857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=426665#post426665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clearly, it's Gwyneth Paltrow's head.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only when a Slasher opens the box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:12:31-08:00","id":426910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=426857#post426857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's only when a Slasher opens the box.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was when a Slasher SENT the box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T02:07:38-08:00","id":427539,"title":"","content":"..and the Hunter opens the box.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would like to believe there are peanuts in the box, the packing variety made of Styrofoam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:49:12-08:00","id":430343,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Watchtowers allow awakening because they transcend the borders between the Phenomenal and the Supernal, after all during a Mystery Play, supernal elements are introduced in the life ofnthe future mage and the Watchtowers are supposed to imitate the way the Ocean Ouroboros awakened the pre-Fall magi, and what was the end of the Ocean Ouroboros except a frontier between the phenomenal and the supernal composed of Supernal Verges and Emanation Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:06:33-08:00","id":430644,"title":"","content":"Technically, every Arcadian Verge can be traced back to an Emanation of Arcadia, which in turn can be traced back to the Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn. The number of potential Supernal Realms is infinite; but only five seem to manifest Verges on Earth: the five associated with the Watchtowers. Coincidence? I doubt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:32:12-07:00","id":440195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=430644#post430644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, every Arcadian Verge can be traced back to an Emanation of Arcadia, which in turn can be traced back to the Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn. The number of potential Supernal Realms is infinite; but only five seem to manifest Verges on Earth: the five associated with the Watchtowers. Coincidence? I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those five Realms are the only regions of the Supernal with permanent Lustrums connected to them (at least by anything resembling a human intelligence), right? It makes sense, then, that they'd be the only ones manifesting Verges accessible to humans in the Material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:51:24-07:00","id":440536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=440195#post440195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those five Realms are the only regions of the Supernal with permanent Lustrums connected to them (at least by anything resembling a human intelligence), right? It makes sense, then, that they'd be the only ones manifesting Verges accessible to humans in the Material.</div> </div> </div> </div>No; every archmaster has a Cintimani which is essentially a region of the Supernal with a permanent Lustrum connected to it. No, a Watchtower is the thing that takes what amounts to an Archmaster\u2019s Cintimani and \u201cbroadcasts\u201d it into the Fallen World, allowing Verges and Mystery Plays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-13-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T07:54:58-08:00","id":1529905,"title":"","content":"After some years, I returned again to the Chronicles of Darkness and found this great thread to answer my questions. It feels wrong to dig it out after the years, but seems even wronger to start a new thread on the same topic and dilute the knowledge. Do I am asking here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415035#post415035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's how I imagined it. Going to Changeling Arcadia vs. 'going to' Supernal Arcadia is &quot;I want to go to the Grand Canyon&quot; vs. &quot;I want to go to geology&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking about this, but it does not fit for the following reasons:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Summoning of Supernal Beings</b> If Supernal Realms are like platonic concepts, how could it have denizen that can be summoned? Are the beings created during the summoning according to their platonic ideal? (The same way as summoning a horse from its platonic form: The ritual would simply create a new instance of horse according to its platonic ideal. It might be corrupted because the ideal cannot fully fit into the Fallen World and because the Abyss corrupts it, but it would essentially be creation de novo)</li> <li><b>The Lower Depths are to the Fallen World what the Fallen</b> This is a sentence from Mage: The Awakening. But it it was literally so, there should be the same gap as between geology and Grand Canyon between the Lower Depths and Fallen World. Yet, the beings from Lower Depths can be summoned and there are Scar Irises to travel there.</li> <li><b>Watchtowers </b>They were created. How do you create a platonic form? (Maybe this is the intentional mystery in the book. It basically says that before the Fall, geology and Grand Canyon were the same category - both existed somehow together. But the split after the Fall is so large that it even seems like a category error how the world looked before - something we cannot imagine. (Am I wrong here?)</li> </ol>Do you know how to explain them in the &quot;Grand Canyon vs geology&quot; theory?<br /> <br /> Also, would you say that Abyss is not a real place, rather it is a concept (or its corruption?) (On the other hand, the Abyssal entities are described as very real..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T09:15:29-08:00","id":1529911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=1529905#post1529905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Summoning of Supernal Beings</b> If Supernal Realms are like platonic concepts, how could it have denizen that can be summoned? Are the beings created during the summoning according to their platonic ideal? (The same way as summoning a horse from its platonic form: The ritual would simply create a new instance of horse according to its platonic ideal. It might be corrupted because the ideal cannot fully fit into the Fallen World and because the Abyss corrupts it, but it would essentially be creation de novo)</div> </div> </div> </div>A Supernal being is too True to exist in the real world; summoning creates a manifestation of that Truth that exists in highly constrained fashion. It may be fundamentally impossible to draw a meaningful distinction between &quot;the destruction of a Supernal being actually destroys it&quot; and &quot;the destruction of a Supernal being prevents that manifestation from interacting with the world in any way that can be perceived by the same characters,&quot; because the Phenomenal World is where time and space matter, but the Supernal is the part of the cosmology outside of reality that describes everything within reality.<br /> <br /> Manifestations of the Supernal in the world exist due to human action and occult confluence, with a side of &quot;parts of the Supernal whose symbolism denotes them as willful actors can willfully act on other symbols.&quot; Focused Mage Sight allows them to be perceived and therefore act upon the observer; there's always a lens or entry point involved when bringing manifest Truth into the world, and the world tends to react in a volatile manner to those manifestations, because it's not built for them to stay there for long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Lower Depths are to the Fallen World what the Fallen</b> This is a sentence from Mage: The Awakening. But it it was literally so, there should be the same gap as between geology and Grand Canyon between the Lower Depths and Fallen World. Yet, the beings from Lower Depths can be summoned and there are Scar Irises to travel there. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Lie of a Lie&quot; aspect is most well-represented by the content in World of Darkness: Inferno, which elaborates on how Infernal demons (denizens of the Lower Depths) are described by True Names and Testaments forged from sin and occultism in the material world and the Invisible Realms; the inhabitants of the myriad Hells find their way into the denser worlds by luck or cunning and insinuate themselves into power through symbolism in a roughly analogous fashion to how mages and archmasters leverage the Supernal, but reliable means of descending into the Depths tend to involve some combination of a reinforced soul and sensory projection/interpretation. Irises into the Depths are largely one-way, and the Inferno defies any consistent description because each observer sees their own intensely personal vision of primordial loathsomeness when they look into an open Hellmouth.<br /> <br /> As with the Supernal, the Lower Depths are coming into the world through interpretive lenses and established contexts; summoning Pazuzu works because a Pazuzu was established in the world by demonologists and/or awful chance for some kernel of Hell to act through, not because the Depths have naturally-occurring storm-demons waiting to be summoned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Watchtowers </b>They were created. How do you create a platonic form? (Maybe this is the intentional mystery in the book. It basically says that before the Fall, geology and Grand Canyon were the same category - both existed somehow together. But the split after the Fall is so large that it even seems like a category error how the world looked before - something we cannot imagine. (Am I wrong here?) </div> </div> </div>The Watchtowers are simultaneously Artifact-subsouls of the Oracles and the Adytons they generate to facilitate Awakenings. They're aspects of divine forces that can't be directly examined without Ascending to their level.<br /> <br /> The Fall is not &quot;the Supernal and the Phenomenal World were the same place,&quot; it's &quot;the connection between the Supernal and the Phenomenal World was more direct/less obscured/subject to less interference.&quot; Aponoia has been described as a smaller-scale version of the Fall, as contradictions and inconsistencies creep in when reality is altered at the fundamental level, and the trajectory of Abyssal involvement is such that things go from &quot;impossible objects and creatures are appearing in the area&quot; to &quot;a nightmarish un-world is insinuating itself into our reality&quot; to &quot;a mage in thrall to these forces of anti-reality cannot meaningfully magically affect things that are not drawn into their personal prison-realm.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, would you say that Abyss is not a real place, rather it is a concept (or its corruption?) (On the other hand, the Abyssal entities are described as very real..) </div> </div> </div>Everything in the cosmology that isn't the Supernal exists. The Abyss and its denizens are distinguished by existing despite it being impossible for them to exist, hence &quot;Paradox&quot; being the term for the errors that involve them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T14:27:41-08:00","id":1529935,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the swift response!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=1529911#post1529911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Supernal being is too True to exist in the real world; summoning creates a manifestation of that Truth that exists in highly constrained fashion. It may be fundamentally impossible to draw a meaningful distinction between &quot;the destruction of a Supernal being actually destroys it&quot; and &quot;the destruction of a Supernal being prevents that manifestation from interacting with the world in any way that can be perceived by the same characters,&quot; because the Phenomenal World is where time and space matter, but the Supernal is the part of the cosmology outside of reality that describes everything within reality.<br /> <br /> Manifestations of the Supernal in the world exist due to human action and occult confluence, with a side of &quot;parts of the Supernal whose symbolism denotes them as willful actors can willfully act on other symbols.&quot; Focused Mage Sight allows them to be perceived and therefore act upon the observer; there's always a lens or entry point involved when bringing manifest Truth into the world, and the world tends to react in a volatile manner to those manifestations, because it's not built for them to stay there for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I remain confused about is this: If Supernal Realms are more like platonic ideals, like the geology rather than the Grand Canyon, do stuff happen there? Do the supernal beings have life of their own that they live? Are they really called from the supernal realm, or just manifested into being according to the respective platonic form? (I imagine, maybe wrongly, platonic ideal of a horse as a non-changing concept of an ideal horse. Something like an equation, unchanging in time - are the supernal realms like this? Or was the talk about the platonic ideals meant in a different sense?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=1529911#post1529911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fall is not &quot;the Supernal and the Phenomenal World were the same place,&quot; it's &quot;the connection between the Supernal and the Phenomenal World was more direct/less obscured/subject to less interference.&quot; Aponoia has been described as a smaller-scale version of the Fall, as contradictions and inconsistencies creep in when reality is altered at the fundamental level</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThank you. This clarifies a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T15:17:36-08:00","id":1529938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=1529935#post1529935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I remain confused about is this: If Supernal Realms are more like platonic ideals, like the geology rather than the Grand Canyon, do stuff happen there? Do the supernal beings have life of their own that they live? Are they really called from the supernal realm, or just manifested into being according to the respective platonic form? (I imagine, maybe wrongly, platonic ideal of a horse as a non-changing concept of an ideal horse. Something like an equation, unchanging in time - are the supernal realms like this? Or was the talk about the platonic ideals meant in a different sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Advanced Supernal Cosmology&quot; section on pages 13-14 of Signs of Sorcery goes over this in some detail, but essentially a Supernal phenomenon is the Truth expressed through the lens of that phenomenon \u2014 a Lustrum is the Supernal putting on a mask of being a singular place and time and collection of actors, interacting with mages through the way of looking at the world that is their Mage Sight. The Supernal describes the world in a fashion not entirely understandable to mortal minds, and the Awakened use its power through a combination of divine intuition and mnemonic aids moreso than understanding of a real ecology like one would find in the Shadow or the Oneiros.<br /> <br /> When we say Supernal Arcadia is to Changeling Arcadia as geology is to the Grand Canyon, we mean that the Supernal is a way of perceiving the world rather than an actual place. Manifestations of the Supernal within reality exist because Supernal knowledge has been manipulated or leveraged to make them so, with varying degrees of success and complication. An Astra is a piece of a god from outside of time and space who interacts with the World of Phenomena in-story within a temporal and spatial context that allows them to do so (largely distinguished from mere hallucination by the confluence of forces that allow physical/spiritual consequences and accurate information to be derived from it), and the Astra enters the world through circumstances within that context that allow a largely indestructible symbolic piece of divinity to exist.<br /> <br /> Since direct audience with Supernal beings requires filters or constructed manifestations, any personal life they have that doesn't interact with the Phenomenal World is narratively indistinguishable for their inner thoughts and the unknowable caprice of otherworldly beings \u2014 you have no way of knowing whether the Old God of the forge that your Moros encountered while Scrutinizing an ancient anvil is asking you to bring the last rose from an otherworldly garden because it had congress with the nymph of that garden or if it's giving you a hint based on its ability to perceive the world without regard for past and future or if it's doing the godly equivalent of being mad at you for something you did in a dream it had or if it's just demonstrating one of the myriad ways the world is full of weird occult bullshit.<br /> <br /> They're perfected forms of assorted subsets of reality operating within the limits of interaction with beings that exist within reality for the sake of conversation. They're eternal and unchanging in the sense that when they change, they've now always been that way as far as the world is concerned \u2014 the four Archigenitors have been the top Exarchs the whole time, even if some records may say that the Nemesis used to be greater in standing than the Chancellor, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-03T20:19:38-08:00","id":1529954,"title":"","content":"Also worth pointing out that Emanations are what the Storyteller uses when he wants to play with the concept of \u201cthe Supernal as a place\u201d; and they are populated by Supernal Entities. That said, Emanations aren't <i>really </i>the Supernal itself; that's why they're called \u201cEmanations\u201d. Entry into the <i>actual</i> Supernal is largely beyond the scope of <b>Mage</b>, because the only way to achieve it without being utterly (and probably retroactively) annihilated is to Ascend. Or to become an Archmaster, which is a lesser version of the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}